# One place for the work that keeps a company running.
Northwind Ops gathers the requests, the runbooks and the on-call rota of an operations team in a single, sovereign workspace.

[Book a walkthrough →](https://example.com/walkthrough){.cta}

---
section: What it does
notes: The four pillars, as cards.
---
## Requests, runbooks, on-call and reporting — in one flow.
Every request lands in a queue, follows a runbook, reaches the person on call and leaves a trace the manager can read on Monday.

::: cards
- Requests | One queue per team, one form per request type. SLAs measured from the first message.
- Runbooks | Step by step, with the checks that must not be skipped. Versioned and reviewed.
- On-call | The rota lives with the runbooks, not in a spreadsheet. Handover notes at every shift.
- Reporting | What came in, what was closed, what waited. A weekly digest read in five minutes.
:::

